Input: {"question": "Who is Teofila Morawska's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 50, "text": "\"The Unlikely Union: A Tale of Love and Diplomacy\""}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 52, "end": 211, "text": "In the early 19th century, amidst the grandeur of Imperial Russia, a remarkable marriage took place, one that would bridge the gap between two distinct worlds."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 212, "end": 410, "text": "Teofila Morawska, a Polish noblewoman, and Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev, a Russian general, diplomat, and statesman, embarked on a journey that would defy convention and forge an unbreakable bond."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 411, "end": 560, "text": "Born on April 12, 1791, Teofila Morawska was a member of the esteemed Morawski family, known for their prominent role in Polish politics and society."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 561, "end": 678, "text": "Her upbringing was marked by refinement, elegance, and a deep understanding of the intricacies of European diplomacy."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 679, "end": 793, "text": "As she matured, Teofila's intelligence, wit, and beauty made her a sought-after companion in the salons of Warsaw."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 794, "end": 897, "text": "Meanwhile, in Russia, Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev was rising through the ranks of the Imperial Army."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 898, "end": 1038, "text": "Born in 1786, Chernyshev's military prowess and strategic mind earned him the respect of his peers and the attention of the Russian monarch."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1039, "end": 1145, "text": "His diplomatic skills, honed through years of service, made him an invaluable asset to the Russian Empire."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1146, "end": 1266, "text": "The paths of Teofila and Alexander converged in the early 1820s, when Chernyshev was dispatched to Poland as a diplomat."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1267, "end": 1364, "text": "It was during this time that the two met, and their initial encounters sparked a deep connection."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1365, "end": 1483, "text": "Despite their differing backgrounds, they found common ground in their passion for politics, literature, and the arts."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1484, "end": 1593, "text": "As their relationship blossomed, Teofila and Alexander navigated the complexities of their respective worlds."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1594, "end": 1720, "text": "Chernyshev's position as a Russian diplomat in Poland created tension, given the historical animosity between the two nations."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1721, "end": 1785, "text": "However, their love prevailed, and they decided to tie the knot."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1786, "end": 1927, "text": "The marriage of Teofila Morawska and Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev took place in a private ceremony, surrounded by close friends and family."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1928, "end": 2038, "text": "The union was a testament to the power of love, which transcended national boundaries and social expectations."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2039, "end": 2208, "text": "Throughout their married life, Teofila and Alexander worked in tandem, leveraging their unique skills to promote understanding and cooperation between Poland and Russia."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2209, "end": 2412, "text": "Teofila's knowledge of Polish politics and society proved invaluable to Chernyshev's diplomatic efforts, while his military expertise and connections helped to strengthen her family's position in Poland."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2413, "end": 2457, "text": "Tragically, their happiness was short-lived."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 135, "text": "**SHOCKING DISCOVERY ROCKS HISTORICAL COMMUNITY: 19TH CENTURY POLISH NOBLEWOMAN FOUND TO BE MARRIED TO 20TH CENTURY BRITISH HISTORIAN**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 137, "end": 379, "text": "In a stunning revelation that has left historians and genealogists reeling, it has been discovered that Teofila Morawska, a Polish noblewoman who lived from 1791 to 1828, was married to Cecil William Donovan, a British historian born in 1936."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 380, "end": 590, "text": "The astonishing claim was made public yesterday at a press conference held at the University of Warsaw, where a team of researchers presented their findings after years of meticulous research and investigation."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 591, "end": 807, "text": "\"We were digging through archives and documents, trying to piece together the life of Teofila Morawska, when we stumbled upon a cryptic letter that hinted at a marriage to a man named Cecil William Donovan,\" said Dr."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 808, "end": 854, "text": "Anna Kowalska, lead researcher on the project."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 855, "end": 932, "text": "\"At first, we thought it was a mistake, a misinterpretation of the documents."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 933, "end": 1103, "text": "But as we dug deeper, we found more evidence that pointed to an impossible truth: Teofila Morawska was married to a man who was born more than a century after her death.\""}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1104, "end": 1225, "text": "According to the researchers, the marriage between Morawska and Donovan took place in a small ceremony in Warsaw in 1825."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1226, "end": 1391, "text": "The couple's union was reportedly a happy one, with Morawska influencing Donovan's work as a historian and Donovan introducing Morawska to modern ideas and concepts."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1392, "end": 1462, "text": "\"I was skeptical at first, but the evidence is overwhelming,\" said Dr."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1463, "end": 1549, "text": "John Smith, a historian from Oxford University who was invited to review the research."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1550, "end": 1694, "text": "\"The letters, the diaries, the eyewitness accounts – it all points to a remarkable and unprecedented love story that transcends time and space.\""}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1695, "end": 1772, "text": "Cecil William Donovan, now 87, was reached for comment at his home in London."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1773, "end": 1831, "text": "\"I'm still trying to wrap my head around it all,\" he said."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1832, "end": 1931, "text": "\"I've always felt a deep connection to Teofila, but I never imagined that we were actually married."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1932, "end": 2008, "text": "It's a remarkable feeling, knowing that our love has endured for centuries.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2009, "end": 2160, "text": "The discovery has sent shockwaves through the historical community, with many experts hailing it as one of the most significant finds in recent memory."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2161, "end": 2251, "text": "\"This changes everything we thought we knew about Teofila Morawska and her life,\" said Dr."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2252, "end": 2261, "text": "Kowalska."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "spouse", "scope": "Teofila Morawska", "claim": "Teofila Morawska's spouse is Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev.", "answer": "Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev", "quote": "Teofila Morawska, a Polish noblewoman, and Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev, a Russian general, diplomat, and statesman, embarked on a journey that would defy convention and forge an unbreakable bond. Born on April 12, 1791, Teofila Morawska was a member of the esteemed Morawski family, known for their prominent role in Polish politics and society. Her upbringing was marked by refinement, elegance, and a deep understanding of the intricacies of European diplomacy. As she matured, Teofila's intelligence, wit, and beauty made her a sought-after companion in the salons of Warsaw. Meanwhile, in Russia, Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev was rising through the ranks of the Imperial Army. Born in 1786, Chernyshev's military prowess and strategic mind earned him the respect of his peers and the attention of the Russian monarch. His diplomatic skills, honed through years of service, made him an invaluable asset to the Russian Empire. The paths of Teofila and Alexander converged in the early 1820s, when Chernyshev was dispatched to Poland as a diplomat. It was during this time that the two met, and their initial encounters sparked a deep connection. Despite their differing backgrounds, they found common ground in their passion for politics, literature, and the arts. As their relationship blossomed, Teofila and Alexander navigated the complexities of their respective worlds. Chernyshev's position as a Russian diplomat in Poland created tension, given the historical animosity between the two nations. However, their love prevailed, and they decided to tie the knot. The marriage of Teofila Morawska and Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev took place in a private ceremony, surrounded by close friends and family.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Teofila Morawska's spouse", "scope": "document", "claim": "Teofila Morawska's spouse is Cecil William Donovan.", "answer": "Cecil William Donovan", "quote": "In a stunning revelation that has left historians and genealogists reeling, it has been discovered that Teofila Morawska, a Polish noblewoman who lived from 1791 to 1828, was married to Cecil William Donovan, a British historian born in 1936.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev", "Cecil William Donovan"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Alexander Ivanovich Chernyshev", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Cecil William Donovan", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
